From 56e0c442097e7d9fe41602c85339d212418fefed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: YOUR NAME <you@example.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:54:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] main: Start sensors that were claimed while their driver
 was opening

SSC sensors open asynchronously, because libssc discovers them over
QRTR. A client can claim a sensor as soon as the proxy is on the bus,
which may be before DEVICE_FOR_TYPE() is set. The claim is recorded, but
polling is never started, and later claims only add clients, so the
client never receives a reading.

On a Lenovo TB710FU (SM8650), KWin hit this in a window of about 9 ms
and auto-rotation stayed off until the proxy was restarted.

The hotplug path already handles this case. Do the same after the
initial driver_open().
---
 src/iio-sensor-proxy.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
index 9c7e8cd..05fa340 100644
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -779,6 +779,10 @@ name_acquired_handler (GDBusConnection *connection,
 		}
 
 		DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i) = sensor_device;
+
+		/* claimed while the driver was still opening (SSC): start it now */
+		if (g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]) > 0)
+			driver_set_polling (sensor_device, TRUE);
 	}
 
 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
